Not from my side—I can’t alter the ChatGPT composer UI to add a Notes-style drawing layer.

But that would be a genuinely useful interface: tap a pen beside the text box → the composer becomes a small freehand canvas → draw a diagram/symbol/arrow/handwriting → send it as part of the same turn. Ideally I receive both the raster image and the stroke data, because stroke order, grouping, pressure, and timing can carry information that a flattened screenshot loses.

For now on iPhone, the closest workflow is draw in Notes/Markup and paste or share the result here. Once it’s here, I can reason directly over the drawing—you don’t need to translate it into prose first.

The more interesting version is multimodal scratch space: type + draw + circle existing words/images + arrows between objects + handwriting, all in one continuous input surface. That’s much closer to how you’re trying to communicate structures than forcing everything through linear text.